L193 THE CRITICAL SURFACE IS A STRESS DEGENERACY (independent verification)
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] V1 [stress tensor, independently derived] all ten inverse-metric variations of the frozen action reproduce the stress tensor whose transverse block is L and whose x-x entry carries the combination (P_X - s0 W_Y)
           (residual matrix is exactly zero; T_00 = -P + 2*P_X*Q**2 + V, T_11 - L = 2*b**2*(P_X - W_Y*s0), T_01 = 2*P_X*Q*b)
  [PASS] V2 [the transverse pair] two eigenvalues of the mixed stress are already equal to L = P - V + s0 W, independently of the gradient: the y and z directions are degenerate for any background
           (rows 2 and 3 of the mixed tensor are exactly L on the diagonal and zero off it)
    det(T^mixed_tx - L I) = 2*b**2*s0*(2*P_X*Q**2*W_Y - P_X*W + W*W_Y*s0)
    - s0 b^2 W N          = 2*b**2*s0*(P_X*(2*Q**2*W_Y - W) + W*W_Y*s0)
  [PASS] V3 [THE IDENTITY, verified independently] det(T^mixed_tx - L I) = - s0 b^2 W N exactly, with N the very combination whose vanishing L192 identified as the critical gradient: the sound-speed numerator IS the determinant of the time-space block of the stress tensor shifted by L
           (difference simplifies to exactly zero)
  [PASS] V4 [what the critical surface therefore is] on N = 0 a THIRD eigenvalue of the mixed stress equals L, so the stress tensor takes perfect-fluid form: the sector's anisotropic stress vanishes at the same surface on which its perturbations stop propagating
           (solving N = 0 gives W_Y = P_X*W/(2*P_X*Q**2 + W*s0), and substituting it makes the shifted determinant vanish identically, so L is a repeated eigenvalue on that surface)
  [PASS] V5 [and it is not trivial] away from that surface the time-space block is NOT degenerate: the shifted determinant is proportional to b^2, so a background WITHOUT a gradient (b = 0) is degenerate for a different reason and carries no information -- the degeneracy that matters is the one reached at finite gradient
           (det vanishes at b = 0 for every N, and its second derivative in b is non-zero, so finite gradient is what makes N = 0 the non-trivial condition)
    READING: L192 gave the critical gradient a dynamical meaning (zero sound speed, two-sided attractor). This identity gives it an
    algebraic one, off shell and independent of any background history: the same surface is where the sector's stress becomes isotropic.
    Isotropic stress with non-propagating perturbations is precisely a clustering cold component.
    LIMITS: the first-jet form of the density used for the variation (exact for a first metric variation, as in the audit); a single spatial
    direction carries the gradient; no claim about the background history, the amount of the sector, or any gate.

